course: dictionary
lesson: 15342
title: Soh, the fifth note
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Soh is a note in music. When you sing do, re, mi, fa, soh, la, ti, do, soh is the fifth note in the row. Singers call this the do-re-mi scale, and it helps you hear how the notes fit together.
explain: «We sang up the scale: do, re, mi, fa, soh.» The last word tells you the name of the fifth note. Count five notes from do and you reach soh. Count as you sing and you will always find it.
explain: Some books spell this note «so» or «sol» instead. They all name the same note, so only the spelling changes. When you see one of these words in a music book, think of the note that comes after fa.
fact: Soh is the fifth note of the do-re-mi scale.
fact: The full scale is do, re, mi, fa, soh, la, ti, do.
fact: Soh can also be spelled so or sol, and they all mean the same note.
fact: In maths, SOH CAH TOA is a memory aid for trigonometry, and that SOH is not a music note.
exercise: Which note is the fifth in the scale do, re, mi, fa, soh, la, ti, do? | Fa | La | Mi | *Soh
exercise: «Sam sang soh, then la, then ti.» Which note comes after soh? | Do | Mi | *La | Fa
exercise: «The music book spelled the note as sol, not soh.» What does sol mean here? | *The same note, spelled differently | A different note, higher than do | A word for sad | A kind of drum
test: Which note comes just before soh in the scale? | Re | Ti | *Fa | La
test: Which is another way to spell the note soh? | *Sol | Sow | Saw | Sew
exam: «The choir sang do, re, mi, fa, soh, la, ti, do, and Ella clapped on soh.» Which note is soh? | *The fifth note | Fa | Mi | Do
